1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,095
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:02,182
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,207 --> 00:00:03,253
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,278 --> 00:00:04,333
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,357 --> 00:00:05,452
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:06,994 --> 00:00:09,458
They say golf is a game of focus.

7
00:00:11,085 --> 00:00:12,797
But to me, it's a game

8
00:00:12,822 --> 00:00:15,202
that teaches us how to stay
with someone long enough.

9
00:00:15,358 --> 00:00:18,103
Eighteen holes are long enough
to see someone smile,

10
00:00:18,128 --> 00:00:20,128
long enough
to see them frustrated,

11
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:23,673
and long enough to know if you
still want to walk beside them.

12
00:00:23,698 --> 00:00:25,643
On the course,
we may each play our own shot,

13
00:00:25,668 --> 00:00:27,896
see things differently,
and stumble on different holes.

14
00:00:27,921 --> 00:00:30,704
But in the end,
we're still heading the same way.

15
00:00:31,061 --> 00:00:32,355
Love is no different.

16
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,525
It's not about hitting
the perfect shot every time.

17
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:36,318
It's about
not leaving each other behind,

18
00:00:36,343 --> 00:00:37,896
even when the ball lands
in a bunker.

19
00:00:37,921 --> 00:00:39,919
Maybe what makes
this game special

20
00:00:39,944 --> 00:00:42,022
isn't the birdies or the eagles,

21
00:00:42,047 --> 00:00:44,535
but hearing someone quietly say,

22
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:47,027
"It's okay. We'll try again.
We'll keep going together."

23
00:00:47,729 --> 00:00:49,842
Because in golf,
you may have to swing alone.

24
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:52,652
But in love, you should never
have to walk alone.

25
00:00:53,091 --> 00:00:56,491
And if you find someone who'll
play every season by your side,

26
00:00:56,516 --> 00:00:58,008
no matter how long the fairway,

27
00:00:58,033 --> 00:00:59,357
your heart will never grow tired.

28
00:01:01,377 --> 00:01:04,552
(Pro Meiji - Jenjira Jinangkul)

29
00:01:10,824 --> 00:01:14,308
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

30
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:16,669
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

31
00:01:16,694 --> 00:01:20,219
♪ It's plain to see ♪

32
00:01:20,737 --> 00:01:22,477
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

33
00:01:22,502 --> 00:01:25,900
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

34
00:01:26,554 --> 00:01:28,371
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

35
00:01:28,396 --> 00:01:31,858
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

36
00:01:32,275 --> 00:01:34,140
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

37
00:01:34,165 --> 00:01:37,000
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

38
00:01:37,025 --> 00:01:38,939
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

39
00:01:38,964 --> 00:01:41,726
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

40
00:01:41,751 --> 00:01:44,643
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

41
00:01:44,668 --> 00:01:48,448
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

42
00:01:48,473 --> 00:01:50,315
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

43
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:53,230
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

44
00:01:53,255 --> 00:01:56,813
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

45
00:01:56,838 --> 00:02:01,550
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

46
00:02:01,575 --> 00:02:03,575
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

47
00:02:05,013 --> 00:02:07,898
I'm thinking of getting
a new manager.

48
00:02:07,923 --> 00:02:09,497
You can't do this to me, Nana.

49
00:02:09,895 --> 00:02:11,710
Besides, we're family.

50
00:02:11,735 --> 00:02:14,269
Family shouldn't
steal from family.

51
00:02:14,371 --> 00:02:15,731
Nut.

52
00:02:15,756 --> 00:02:19,176
I have six months to
make this place profitable again.

53
00:02:19,201 --> 00:02:22,905
So I need someone experienced
and trustworthy to help me.

54
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:24,104
Wait. Me?

55
00:02:24,155 --> 00:02:25,806
Dark chocolate.
It's a little bitter.

56
00:02:25,831 --> 00:02:27,520
It might taste bitter at first,

57
00:02:27,545 --> 00:02:29,905
but I think there's
a little sweetness underneath.

58
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,495
Kind of like someone I know.
Acts all tough,

59
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,979
but she's secretly sweet.

60
00:02:38,247 --> 00:02:40,795
Do you know
why I gave you two weeks

61
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,820
to conquer the hardest hole?

62
00:02:43,901 --> 00:02:45,689
To put pressure on me?

63
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:47,261
No.

64
00:02:47,657 --> 00:02:51,275
I wanted to see
how long you'd stick with it.

65
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,237
Because if you're only doing this
to beat me,

66
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:54,915
you might give up halfway.

67
00:02:56,601 --> 00:02:59,553
But if you're doing it
to overcome your own limits,

68
00:03:01,842 --> 00:03:03,831
then this hole
won't just be a condition.

69
00:03:05,322 --> 00:03:07,322
It'll prove that

70
00:03:08,061 --> 00:03:09,795
no matter what comes your way,

71
00:03:10,677 --> 00:03:12,383
you won't give up easily.

72
00:03:13,229 --> 00:03:14,809
And you won't run from it.

73
00:03:15,373 --> 00:03:17,690
You'll be ready to give it
everything you've got.

74
00:03:18,746 --> 00:03:20,076
And if you pull it off,

75
00:03:20,322 --> 00:03:22,195
I'll give you my full support.

76
00:03:33,862 --> 00:03:37,220
Thank you, everyone,
for coming to support me.

77
00:03:37,754 --> 00:03:38,794
You got this!

78
00:03:38,999 --> 00:03:41,266
Give it your all, Miss Nana!

79
00:03:41,543 --> 00:03:43,400
What I'm about to do

80
00:03:43,425 --> 00:03:46,135
isn't just about
meeting Pro Vee's challenge.

81
00:03:48,277 --> 00:03:50,609
If I'm going to run this course,

82
00:03:51,045 --> 00:03:53,823
I want to start by
showing everyone

83
00:03:54,003 --> 00:03:58,067
that I'm serious and ready
to face whatever comes my way.

84
00:03:58,614 --> 00:04:02,167
It means so much
to have everyone behind me.

85
00:04:14,761 --> 00:04:16,596
No matter how it turns out,

86
00:04:16,889 --> 00:04:18,889
I want everyone to know

87
00:04:20,394 --> 00:04:22,203
that I really gave it my all.

88
00:04:30,926 --> 00:04:33,789
Wow! Great shot!

89
00:04:33,948 --> 00:04:36,559
That was beautiful, Miss Nana!

90
00:04:48,349 --> 00:04:49,694
Beautiful.

91
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:02,453
I called
this urgent meeting today

92
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,215
because I have an announcement.

93
00:05:06,269 --> 00:05:07,961
Starting today,

94
00:05:09,127 --> 00:05:13,398
March will be
taking over as manager

95
00:05:13,423 --> 00:05:15,121
of the Royal Green Golf Club.

96
00:05:21,282 --> 00:05:24,785
As for Mr. Thiti,
who's held the position for years

97
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:26,303
with nothing to show for it,

98
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:29,743
I've transferred him
to manage my hotel in Chiang Rai.

99
00:05:40,243 --> 00:05:43,267
Why does everyone
look so surprised?

100
00:05:43,775 --> 00:05:45,227
A round of applause, please.

101
00:05:52,958 --> 00:05:54,481
Surely you can do
better than that.

102
00:05:55,033 --> 00:05:58,041
Let's show some
Royal Green spirit.

103
00:06:21,102 --> 00:06:22,794
Nice ball position.

104
00:06:25,495 --> 00:06:28,960
Nana's really something.

105
00:06:29,183 --> 00:06:31,723
It's not often we get to see
the little one's fighting spirit.

106
00:06:31,748 --> 00:06:33,033
She takes after her father.

107
00:06:33,686 --> 00:06:35,927
I mean
her determination and drive.

108
00:06:35,952 --> 00:06:37,952
Just look at her eyes, sir.

109
00:06:38,588 --> 00:06:39,731
Oh, thanks.

110
00:06:39,852 --> 00:06:42,218
Beginner's luck, maybe?

111
00:06:42,282 --> 00:06:44,022
One shot
and you're all impressed already?

112
00:06:44,047 --> 00:06:45,626
Hole 7 isn't easy, you know.

113
00:06:47,017 --> 00:06:49,585
Come on, August.
Show her some support.

114
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:52,167
If you can do this, Nana,

115
00:06:52,421 --> 00:06:54,731
I'll do my part to help you
turn this course around.

116
00:06:59,766 --> 00:07:01,603
Give it your all, Miss Nana!

117
00:07:16,318 --> 00:07:17,986
Oh! Into the water!

118
00:07:19,266 --> 00:07:20,281
Whoa.

119
00:07:31,123 --> 00:07:33,582
There's a one-stroke penalty
for hitting it into the water.

120
00:07:33,607 --> 00:07:35,352
So you're already
at three strokes.

121
00:07:51,144 --> 00:07:53,293
Oh, she gets another ball.

122
00:07:53,318 --> 00:07:56,128
I thought she'd have to
hit it out of the water.

123
00:07:56,859 --> 00:07:58,537
The rules give you
a one-stroke penalty,

124
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:00,235
then you can play again
from the same spot,

125
00:08:00,401 --> 00:08:03,035
or drop a ball
near where it went in.

126
00:08:03,139 --> 00:08:04,139
I see.

127
00:08:04,164 --> 00:08:06,339
Don't lose heart,
my little fighter.

128
00:08:07,338 --> 00:08:09,477
Water down.
How about the sand next, Nana?

129
00:08:09,502 --> 00:08:11,707
Hey! Come on!

130
00:08:11,837 --> 00:08:13,697
Let's give the golfer
some peace and quiet, please.

131
00:08:13,722 --> 00:08:15,538
Me? He's the one.

132
00:08:15,897 --> 00:08:17,207
Take it down a notch.

133
00:08:20,271 --> 00:08:22,579
Focus. Don't get distracted.

134
00:08:22,604 --> 00:08:24,419
Forget the last shot.
It's already behind you.

135
00:08:46,739 --> 00:08:51,169
Oh, come on!
It went into the sand!

136
00:09:07,958 --> 00:09:09,669
Stay calm, Nana.

137
00:09:09,732 --> 00:09:12,111
If this one doesn't go in,
you'll still have another chance.

138
00:09:12,438 --> 00:09:13,843
Now that's positive thinking.

139
00:09:17,666 --> 00:09:19,168
Remember to allow for the wind.

140
00:09:26,749 --> 00:09:28,233
Stay calm.

141
00:09:28,367 --> 00:09:30,272
Focus on the shot ahead.

142
00:09:50,741 --> 00:09:53,760
- Whoa!
- Amazing!

143
00:09:53,785 --> 00:09:55,230
Great shot!

144
00:10:40,739 --> 00:10:41,794
Well done.

145
00:10:42,578 --> 00:10:45,030
Six strokes on a par-five hole.

146
00:10:45,055 --> 00:10:47,864
That's a bogey,
two strokes under the limit.

147
00:10:47,889 --> 00:10:48,896
You did it.

148
00:10:48,921 --> 00:10:51,998
Yay! I did it! I did it!

149
00:10:52,023 --> 00:10:55,793
Not "choo-choo" this time.
Choo! One bogey!

150
00:10:56,129 --> 00:10:57,797
See? When you really
put your mind to it,

151
00:10:57,822 --> 00:10:59,361
nothing's too difficult.

152
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:03,272
Well done, sweetheart.

153
00:11:04,821 --> 00:11:06,218
Tell you what.

154
00:11:06,626 --> 00:11:07,925
Let's head up to the clubhouse.

155
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:11,120
I'll have Chef Queen
whip up something special

156
00:11:11,145 --> 00:11:12,747
to celebrate.

157
00:11:13,331 --> 00:11:15,900
You got it!
I'm going all out today!

158
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:18,362
A full spread!
You hit plenty onto the green,

159
00:11:18,477 --> 00:11:21,033
so how about some green curry
with tender grass shoots?

160
00:11:21,058 --> 00:11:23,058
- Whoa!
- Yay!

161
00:11:23,083 --> 00:11:24,330
Come on. Let's go eat.

162
00:11:25,162 --> 00:11:27,064
You guys go on ahead.

163
00:11:27,089 --> 00:11:29,216
I'd like a quick word
with Pro Vee.

164
00:11:29,747 --> 00:11:32,037
Oh, okay.
We'll go on ahead, then.

165
00:11:32,062 --> 00:11:35,523
- Okay.
- Green curry! Green curry!

166
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,121
That was amazing.

167
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:49,547
Your swing is steadier,
and your timing has improved.

168
00:11:49,699 --> 00:11:51,438
Especially your approach shots.

169
00:11:51,802 --> 00:11:53,743
In just two weeks,

170
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:56,609
you couldn't have improved
this much on your own.

171
00:11:57,650 --> 00:11:58,713
You knew?

172
00:11:59,868 --> 00:12:00,895
I could tell.

173
00:12:01,768 --> 00:12:03,228
I'm sorry.

174
00:12:03,387 --> 00:12:05,167
It's not that I don't trust you

175
00:12:05,192 --> 00:12:06,779
or think you're a bad coach.

176
00:12:06,961 --> 00:12:08,638
I just really
wanted to get this right,

177
00:12:08,663 --> 00:12:10,316
and I didn't have much time.

178
00:12:10,341 --> 00:12:13,446
So I secretly got some help
from a pro at another course.

179
00:12:13,471 --> 00:12:14,549
Good.

180
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:17,125
You're not mad at me, are you?

181
00:12:17,886 --> 00:12:19,130
Why would I be?

182
00:12:19,347 --> 00:12:21,347
If you just waited for me
to teach you everything,

183
00:12:21,666 --> 00:12:23,218
I'd be the one
who should feel bad

184
00:12:23,243 --> 00:12:25,005
for not giving you enough time.

185
00:12:25,283 --> 00:12:26,765
A true fighter

186
00:12:26,789 --> 00:12:29,389
doesn't choose the path
that keeps everyone comfortable.

187
00:12:29,549 --> 00:12:32,972
They choose the path
that makes them better,

188
00:12:32,997 --> 00:12:34,575
as long as
they play by the rules.

189
00:12:35,307 --> 00:12:37,360
Thank you for understanding.

190
00:12:38,329 --> 00:12:39,829
You didn't beat me today.

191
00:12:40,169 --> 00:12:41,927
You beat the goal
you set for yourself.

192
00:12:42,951 --> 00:12:44,761
Just like you told me,

193
00:12:45,022 --> 00:12:48,418
I have to keep taking on
the smaller challenges first.

194
00:12:48,443 --> 00:12:50,381
Then when I face
something bigger,

195
00:12:50,406 --> 00:12:51,803
I won't be afraid.

196
00:12:52,637 --> 00:12:55,329
Well done.
So, who did you train with?

197
00:12:57,446 --> 00:12:59,501
Pro Jin at the Royal Green.

198
00:13:03,857 --> 00:13:06,730
She's good.
You should bring her over here.

199
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:12,555
If she can help you improve
that much in so little time,

200
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,340
this course could use
someone like her.

201
00:13:20,114 --> 00:13:23,986
No single person
can make this course better.

202
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:27,681
It'll improve if we keep bringing
talented people on board.

203
00:13:28,323 --> 00:13:30,181
That'll push the rest of us

204
00:13:30,389 --> 00:13:31,855
to keep improving too.

205
00:13:34,243 --> 00:13:36,030
Do you really mean that?

206
00:13:38,377 --> 00:13:40,251
I taught you
to overcome yourself,

207
00:13:40,276 --> 00:13:41,998
not to limit yourself.

208
00:13:51,394 --> 00:13:52,405
Okay.

209
00:14:00,629 --> 00:14:02,354
I'm here to make some changes.

210
00:14:03,188 --> 00:14:06,213
To make this course
truly number one.

211
00:14:08,251 --> 00:14:10,441
Come on,
let's get some energy in here!

212
00:14:11,131 --> 00:14:12,456
Fire yourselves up!

213
00:14:13,057 --> 00:14:15,595
Unleash that beast inside you!
Come on!

214
00:14:23,861 --> 00:14:25,027
Follow my lead.

215
00:14:32,283 --> 00:14:33,387
Very good.

216
00:14:34,308 --> 00:14:39,207
That's it. This is the kind of
new culture we need at this club,

217
00:14:39,524 --> 00:14:41,131
where we motivate one another.

218
00:14:44,669 --> 00:14:46,114
Oh, I almost forgot.

219
00:14:46,430 --> 00:14:49,751
Please let everyone know
that from now on,

220
00:14:50,141 --> 00:14:52,136
I'll be cutting caddy pay by 50%.

221
00:14:52,581 --> 00:14:55,438
They already make plenty
from tips anyway.

222
00:14:56,070 --> 00:14:57,071
Don't they?

223
00:14:59,978 --> 00:15:04,903
And every pro will have a sales
target for lesson packages.

224
00:15:06,173 --> 00:15:07,602
We're not salespeople.

225
00:15:09,149 --> 00:15:11,721
No, but you can learn.

226
00:15:12,524 --> 00:15:13,971
It'll make you more well-rounded.

227
00:15:14,588 --> 00:15:16,963
There's more to the job
than playing and teaching golf.

228
00:15:25,042 --> 00:15:28,784
Each pro will be expected
to meet their assigned target.

229
00:15:29,490 --> 00:15:32,726
Each of you will also have
a different income cap,

230
00:15:33,562 --> 00:15:34,665
based on your performance.

231
00:15:35,610 --> 00:15:37,542
Any earnings above that cap

232
00:15:37,987 --> 00:15:40,177
will go entirely to the club.

233
00:15:41,318 --> 00:15:44,731
And if you compete in tournaments
or receive sponsorships,

234
00:15:45,159 --> 00:15:48,387
the club will take 50%
of that income as well.

235
00:15:48,923 --> 00:15:51,437
After all, you're using
the club's reputation

236
00:15:51,462 --> 00:15:53,215
to make money for yourselves.

237
00:15:55,783 --> 00:15:57,540
Isn't it the club

238
00:15:57,565 --> 00:16:00,191
that relies on its pros'
reputation to bring in customers?

239
00:16:02,549 --> 00:16:05,944
Sports have to succeed
as a business

240
00:16:05,969 --> 00:16:07,396
if they're going to survive.

241
00:16:08,882 --> 00:16:10,092
From now on,

242
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:15,229
your skills will be measured
by the value they generate.

243
00:16:19,874 --> 00:16:20,889
Thank you.

244
00:16:31,064 --> 00:16:33,609
Oh, Miss Nana! Stop right there!

245
00:16:33,634 --> 00:16:35,457
Why didn't you let
the staff carry that?

246
00:16:35,483 --> 00:16:37,312
So I can understand
what it's like for them

247
00:16:37,337 --> 00:16:38,765
and what they have to deal with.

248
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:42,261
No, no! Put that down.
Put it down, Miss Nana!

249
00:16:42,562 --> 00:16:44,921
Absolutely not!
Please stop, Miss Nana.

250
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,759
If your father
finds out about this,

251
00:16:47,784 --> 00:16:51,221
we'll all be packing our bags
and getting fired!

252
00:16:51,246 --> 00:16:52,715
Everyone's already left.

253
00:16:53,078 --> 00:16:57,334
Everyone keeps telling me
how amazing your food is.

254
00:16:58,629 --> 00:17:00,110
Oh, I know.

255
00:17:00,135 --> 00:17:02,277
Everybody says so.

256
00:17:02,578 --> 00:17:06,663
I've got the looks
and the cooking skills.

257
00:17:06,688 --> 00:17:08,276
A perfect recipe to keep a man...

258
00:17:09,515 --> 00:17:12,322
What man? I don't have one.
Never mind.

259
00:17:13,237 --> 00:17:14,687
Then let me do the dishes.

260
00:17:14,711 --> 00:17:18,612
Oh, Miss Nana! If those hands
are going to get calluses,

261
00:17:18,821 --> 00:17:21,563
let them be from a golf club!

262
00:17:22,110 --> 00:17:23,126
Queen!

263
00:17:24,011 --> 00:17:27,940
But I have something
for you today.

264
00:17:34,184 --> 00:17:37,822
Cake! Because Miss Nana here
was totally...

265
00:17:37,987 --> 00:17:42,368
crushed it, legit, banana split!

266
00:17:42,393 --> 00:17:44,393
- Of course!
- Go on, have some.

267
00:17:48,990 --> 00:17:53,585
Mmm... ahhh!

268
00:17:55,052 --> 00:17:56,537
Adorable!

269
00:17:56,593 --> 00:18:00,523
So easy to please.
That's my darling girl!

270
00:18:00,563 --> 00:18:02,130
Queen...

271
00:18:02,591 --> 00:18:06,323
Does Pro Vee usually
get her feelings hurt easily?

272
00:18:06,348 --> 00:18:08,509
Or dwell on little things?

273
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,291
I don't think so.

274
00:18:12,712 --> 00:18:15,141
If anything,
she's pretty straightforward.

275
00:18:15,714 --> 00:18:17,040
Why? Did something happen?

276
00:18:19,455 --> 00:18:22,252
Come here, Miss Nana.
Sit down.

277
00:18:22,545 --> 00:18:26,327
Come on, sit, sit!

278
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:28,840
You can't ask her to come here.

279
00:18:28,865 --> 00:18:30,190
Those two don't get along.

280
00:18:31,405 --> 00:18:32,604
Who doesn't?

281
00:18:32,727 --> 00:18:35,727
Pro Vee and Pro Jin!

282
00:18:36,579 --> 00:18:38,865
I knew it.

283
00:18:38,890 --> 00:18:40,646
Pro Vee was acting strange.

284
00:18:41,336 --> 00:18:44,599
What happened between them?
Why don't they get along?

285
00:18:45,557 --> 00:18:48,033
I can't quite remem...
Oh!

286
00:18:48,487 --> 00:18:50,424
I'll look it up for you. Here.

287
00:18:52,937 --> 00:18:56,859
Found it! This is the article.

288
00:18:56,884 --> 00:19:00,275
"Two rising stars
of Thai women's golf,

289
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,105
rivals since their junior days,

290
00:19:02,144 --> 00:19:04,222
Venus and Jinny,

291
00:19:04,247 --> 00:19:06,658
meet as professionals
for the first time.

292
00:19:06,855 --> 00:19:09,420
All eyes are on the two

293
00:19:09,888 --> 00:19:11,547
to see who will come out on top."

294
00:19:16,219 --> 00:19:18,841
- There's nothing here, Queen.
- Oh.

295
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,447
Not juicy enough for you?

296
00:19:22,114 --> 00:19:23,877
Give me that.
I'll find something.

297
00:19:26,078 --> 00:19:29,654
Here! This one's got a photo too.

298
00:19:30,918 --> 00:19:32,585
Pro Jin was disqualified,

299
00:19:32,935 --> 00:19:35,686
even though they'd been
neck and neck the whole match.

300
00:19:35,711 --> 00:19:38,591
- Looks like she's about to cry.
- Exactly.

301
00:19:38,803 --> 00:19:42,173
That's the match where something
happened between them.

302
00:19:42,449 --> 00:19:45,185
I honestly don't remember
the details,

303
00:19:45,210 --> 00:19:48,643
but basically, they were close
friends who trained together.

304
00:19:48,668 --> 00:19:50,865
Then the first time
they competed against each other,

305
00:19:51,302 --> 00:19:52,713
something happened.

306
00:19:52,738 --> 00:19:55,665
Then I'd better
ask Pro Vee about it.

307
00:19:55,963 --> 00:19:59,035
- Good thing I asked you first.
- Mm-hmm.

308
00:19:59,512 --> 00:20:01,219
Wait...

309
00:20:01,243 --> 00:20:04,824
I already had Belle approach
Pro Jin about joining us.

310
00:20:05,503 --> 00:20:07,013
You already approached her?

311
00:20:09,888 --> 00:20:12,827
Miss Nana, whatever you do,

312
00:20:12,852 --> 00:20:15,178
please think of Pro Vee.

313
00:20:22,845 --> 00:20:26,836
Looks like I'm going to need
your help again, Queen.

314
00:20:28,598 --> 00:20:29,621
With...?

315
00:20:43,003 --> 00:20:44,050
What is it?

316
00:20:44,669 --> 00:20:47,195
Wow, that's a little curt,
Pro Vee.

317
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:48,959
Could you sweeten it up a little?

318
00:20:50,396 --> 00:20:54,906
What is it, my dear Nana?
Is that sweet enough for you?

319
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:57,991
Much better. I like it.

320
00:20:58,897 --> 00:21:01,040
So, what is it, dear?

321
00:21:01,777 --> 00:21:05,006
Have you had dinner yet,
dear Pro Vee?

322
00:21:05,133 --> 00:21:07,637
Not yet. Why, dear?

323
00:21:09,118 --> 00:21:12,102
Chef Queen prepared
a whole dinner spread

324
00:21:12,127 --> 00:21:14,009
to celebrate my little victory.

325
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:16,833
- Oh, actually, I don't...
- Seven o'clock sharp.

326
00:21:17,411 --> 00:21:20,069
- But...
- You have an hour and a half.

327
00:21:20,106 --> 00:21:22,119
See you then.
Make yourself pretty!

328
00:21:40,826 --> 00:21:43,000
Hello, Pro Jin. I'm Belle.

329
00:21:44,055 --> 00:21:45,865
You're two minutes late.

330
00:21:46,174 --> 00:21:48,022
- Oh, there was traffic...
- That's all right.

331
00:21:48,426 --> 00:21:49,990
Everyone has their reasons.

332
00:21:50,130 --> 00:21:52,582
I just wanted you to know
that you were late.

333
00:21:53,018 --> 00:21:54,082
Please, have a seat.

334
00:21:57,559 --> 00:21:59,399
Let's get straight to business.

335
00:22:00,454 --> 00:22:01,956
Starting from 100,

336
00:22:01,981 --> 00:22:03,613
keep subtracting seven for me.

337
00:22:03,869 --> 00:22:06,083
Is this part of
the job interview?

338
00:22:09,283 --> 00:22:15,185
Ninety-three, eighty-six,
seventy-nine, seventy-two...

339
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:16,738
Okay, that's enough.

340
00:22:19,376 --> 00:22:21,074
Shall we order first?

341
00:22:46,628 --> 00:22:47,777
You're here.

342
00:22:52,141 --> 00:22:54,729
Did you really
have to dress up this much?

343
00:22:55,063 --> 00:22:56,779
Well, since I got back,

344
00:22:56,804 --> 00:22:59,069
I haven't worn any of the clothes
I brought back with me.

345
00:22:59,187 --> 00:23:01,187
So I thought
I might as well tonight.

346
00:23:01,632 --> 00:23:02,643
Do I look pretty?

347
00:23:04,374 --> 00:23:05,384
You do.

348
00:23:11,606 --> 00:23:13,827
The dress or me?

349
00:23:17,892 --> 00:23:20,008
Both.

350
00:23:23,043 --> 00:23:25,907
Can we eat now?

351
00:23:25,932 --> 00:23:27,932
Or do I need to go change first?

352
00:23:28,654 --> 00:23:31,363
No need. You look pretty in that.

353
00:23:31,879 --> 00:23:34,375
Just a little less
pretty than me. Sit down.

354
00:23:42,392 --> 00:23:43,797
Do you drink?

355
00:23:44,734 --> 00:23:45,870
A little.

356
00:23:54,475 --> 00:23:55,927
Here, let me help.

357
00:24:21,145 --> 00:24:25,439
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

358
00:24:26,167 --> 00:24:31,377
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

359
00:24:31,402 --> 00:24:35,880
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

360
00:24:36,486 --> 00:24:40,965
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

361
00:24:41,585 --> 00:24:46,655
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

362
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:50,896
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

363
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:54,894
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

364
00:24:54,919 --> 00:24:57,380
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

365
00:24:57,405 --> 00:25:03,019
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

366
00:25:03,044 --> 00:25:06,111
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

367
00:25:06,136 --> 00:25:10,924
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

368
00:25:11,546 --> 00:25:14,007
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

369
00:25:14,032 --> 00:25:17,559
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

370
00:25:21,130 --> 00:25:23,378
Quick-fire questions
from here on out.

371
00:25:25,133 --> 00:25:26,149
Huh?

372
00:25:26,174 --> 00:25:27,530
- One or two?
- What do you mean?

373
00:25:27,555 --> 00:25:28,968
- Just answer.
- One.

374
00:25:28,993 --> 00:25:31,265
- Bedroom or bathroom?
- Bathroom.

375
00:25:31,290 --> 00:25:33,550
- Left or right?
- Right.

376
00:25:33,575 --> 00:25:36,484
- Morning or night?
- Night.

377
00:25:36,509 --> 00:25:38,430
- Black or pink?
- Pink.

378
00:25:39,725 --> 00:25:43,002
- Savory or sweet?
- I like both.

379
00:25:43,027 --> 00:25:44,330
Pick one, please.

380
00:25:45,233 --> 00:25:47,191
- Sweet.
- Very good.

381
00:25:47,866 --> 00:25:50,511
- Are we on a game show now?
- Moving on.

382
00:25:50,606 --> 00:25:53,444
The next few questions
are rather personal.

383
00:25:53,469 --> 00:25:55,677
You don't have to answer
if you're uncomfortable.

384
00:25:56,479 --> 00:25:58,108
Current relationship status?

385
00:25:58,133 --> 00:26:02,857
Single, married, divorced,
talking to someone...

386
00:26:03,029 --> 00:26:05,068
or secretly got yourself
a golden retriever?

387
00:26:05,433 --> 00:26:06,441
Single.

388
00:26:06,679 --> 00:26:09,079
How often do you clean your room?

389
00:26:09,623 --> 00:26:12,209
Every day, every other day,
once a week?

390
00:26:12,272 --> 00:26:14,989
It varies,
but I never let it get dirty.

391
00:26:15,217 --> 00:26:16,262
Do you have any pets?

392
00:26:16,287 --> 00:26:18,392
I'd like a cat,
but I don't have the time.

393
00:26:18,417 --> 00:26:21,155
How long does your period
usually last?

394
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:22,388
Five to seven days.

395
00:26:22,413 --> 00:26:25,636
Any irritability, mood swings,
or depression?

396
00:26:25,661 --> 00:26:27,304
No. I'm usually fine.

397
00:26:27,759 --> 00:26:28,973
Last question.

398
00:26:29,310 --> 00:26:32,643
What do you think
makes a woman beautiful?

399
00:26:36,314 --> 00:26:37,960
The way she thinks.

400
00:26:38,825 --> 00:26:41,278
Okay. That's all my questions.

401
00:26:41,829 --> 00:26:45,792
Aren't you going to ask about
golf or my experience?

402
00:26:46,094 --> 00:26:49,591
No. I've already done
my research on you.

403
00:26:49,616 --> 00:26:51,401
I have no doubts
about your qualifications.

404
00:26:51,539 --> 00:26:53,205
Can you start tomorrow?

405
00:26:54,054 --> 00:26:56,922
- Tomorrow?
- That's what I just said.

406
00:26:58,685 --> 00:26:59,835
All right.

407
00:27:00,475 --> 00:27:01,711
And the salary...

408
00:27:01,736 --> 00:27:03,655
I know you have a number in mind.

409
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:05,466
So do we.

410
00:27:05,609 --> 00:27:08,869
We can talk openly
when you sign tomorrow.

411
00:27:10,201 --> 00:27:11,341
Okay.

412
00:27:11,366 --> 00:27:14,153
Then I'll see you at Goodview
at 10 tomorrow.

413
00:27:14,178 --> 00:27:16,178
Make sure you get enough rest.

414
00:27:18,003 --> 00:27:20,665
You look a little dark
under the eyes.

415
00:27:31,259 --> 00:27:32,904
Drink. Cheers!

416
00:27:34,399 --> 00:27:35,796
Cheers.

417
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:37,447
Haven't you had enough?

418
00:27:37,940 --> 00:27:40,385
No, not yet.
Cheers!

419
00:27:43,134 --> 00:27:45,305
We have to celebrate
the good things.

420
00:27:46,378 --> 00:27:49,665
There'll be plenty more
to celebrate. No need to rush.

421
00:27:51,536 --> 00:27:56,440
No. We should celebrate
the little wins along the way

422
00:27:56,563 --> 00:27:58,299
before we reach our goal.

423
00:27:59,610 --> 00:28:02,971
And what's your ultimate goal?

424
00:28:04,229 --> 00:28:09,057
To go back to France
and live the life I want.

425
00:28:09,344 --> 00:28:13,039
You know, I don't like pressure.

426
00:28:13,064 --> 00:28:15,777
I don't want
to prove myself to anyone.

427
00:28:18,054 --> 00:28:20,333
If I'm being completely honest,

428
00:28:20,897 --> 00:28:23,938
what my grandpa and dad built

429
00:28:23,963 --> 00:28:26,846
is more than enough for
the family to live comfortably.

430
00:28:27,156 --> 00:28:32,311
No one needs to prove themselves
in three months or six.

431
00:28:32,336 --> 00:28:34,807
If it doesn't work, sell it.
Why keep carrying the burden?

432
00:28:34,832 --> 00:28:36,291
Don't you think?

433
00:28:44,727 --> 00:28:47,305
Still, I'm glad I have you.

434
00:28:48,068 --> 00:28:50,234
What's that got to do
with anything?

435
00:28:50,259 --> 00:28:53,508
Because you're the reason I...

436
00:28:58,191 --> 00:29:00,104
Mm... you know.

437
00:29:06,931 --> 00:29:11,045
Let's just say I'm really glad
I have you.

438
00:29:11,070 --> 00:29:14,594
Otherwise, I wouldn't care
about any of this.

439
00:29:14,991 --> 00:29:18,743
And I know my dad
wouldn't really be cruel enough

440
00:29:18,768 --> 00:29:21,118
to cut me off if I failed.

441
00:29:22,376 --> 00:29:25,408
Then why keep
putting yourself through this?

442
00:29:25,975 --> 00:29:29,374
Maybe because of
what Dad said that day.

443
00:29:30,281 --> 00:29:32,543
If I don't start fighting now,

444
00:29:32,912 --> 00:29:34,989
how will I ever fight
for anything?

445
00:29:36,898 --> 00:29:39,979
I've never had to fight
for anything in my life.

446
00:29:41,027 --> 00:29:43,890
Whenever I had to compete
or fight for something,

447
00:29:43,915 --> 00:29:46,788
I'd choose to run away
or back down.

448
00:29:46,813 --> 00:29:48,934
I'd always find a way out.

449
00:29:49,259 --> 00:29:51,259
And life was so much easier
that way.

450
00:29:54,715 --> 00:29:58,781
A life without having to compete
or fight for anything...

451
00:29:59,031 --> 00:30:01,270
- I wonder what that's like.
- Easy.

452
00:30:01,754 --> 00:30:05,645
So easy. The easiest.

453
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:08,720
Sooo easy.

454
00:30:15,904 --> 00:30:19,239
Hey! You're out just like that?

455
00:31:02,874 --> 00:31:04,543
How are you getting home, Belle?

456
00:31:04,568 --> 00:31:05,678
I'm booking a ride.

457
00:31:06,672 --> 00:31:08,498
It's pretty hard
to get a ride around here.

458
00:31:08,851 --> 00:31:10,907
Where are you headed?
Want to ride with me?

459
00:31:11,589 --> 00:31:14,082
It's okay. I'm sure a driver
will accept eventually.

460
00:31:14,849 --> 00:31:17,866
Hmm... Don't waste your time.

461
00:31:18,453 --> 00:31:20,025
If you feel bad about it,

462
00:31:20,579 --> 00:31:22,243
you can just pay me by the mile.

463
00:31:24,125 --> 00:31:27,398
Then I'll treat this like
I booked a ride with you.

464
00:31:30,916 --> 00:31:32,238
I'll give you directions.

465
00:32:00,299 --> 00:32:02,789
Sit here for a bit.
You're really drunk.

466
00:32:03,574 --> 00:32:05,710
Drunk? Do I look drunk?

467
00:32:05,862 --> 00:32:08,174
Yes. Very.

468
00:32:09,341 --> 00:32:12,626
But I don't think I'm drunk.

469
00:32:16,242 --> 00:32:19,038
You're still denying it?
Want some water?

470
00:32:20,434 --> 00:32:23,290
Then I'll have
a glass of champagne

471
00:32:23,315 --> 00:32:25,641
to prove I'm not drunk.

472
00:32:30,456 --> 00:32:36,215
Seven par... one choo-choo...

473
00:32:36,656 --> 00:32:41,235
Choo-choo!
Chugga-chugga, choo-choo!

474
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:44,353
Here.

475
00:32:45,099 --> 00:32:46,299
Thank you.

476
00:32:48,524 --> 00:32:50,438
Hey! You spilled it all!

477
00:32:50,463 --> 00:32:51,923
Look, you're all wet.

478
00:32:52,203 --> 00:32:54,195
It's wet,
so it has to come off, Pro Vee.

479
00:32:54,267 --> 00:32:55,458
- Hey!
- It's wet.

480
00:32:56,186 --> 00:32:57,509
You're not taking it off here.

481
00:32:57,874 --> 00:33:00,152
You can take it off
when you shower.

482
00:33:01,506 --> 00:33:04,556
But it's wet, Pro Vee.
I have to take it off.

483
00:33:04,581 --> 00:33:06,581
- No, you don't.
- But it's wet...

484
00:33:14,741 --> 00:33:19,370
Gorgeous Pro Vee and
the cutest little golf heiress...

485
00:33:19,395 --> 00:33:22,263
Now, how should this scene end,
Pro Vee?

486
00:33:24,952 --> 00:33:26,438
You're really drunk.

487
00:33:28,287 --> 00:33:31,123
Then you have to take care of me.

488
00:33:31,148 --> 00:33:34,180
Drunk girls need someone
to take care of them.

489
00:33:50,503 --> 00:33:51,774
You can drop me off here.

490
00:33:53,870 --> 00:33:56,123
I'll scan to pay you
for the ride.

491
00:33:56,591 --> 00:33:57,819
Really, you don't have to.

492
00:33:58,335 --> 00:34:01,184
I do. I always keep my word.

493
00:34:03,425 --> 00:34:06,677
My phone's dead, and I don't
remember my account number.

494
00:34:07,343 --> 00:34:08,940
You can owe me for now.

495
00:34:09,618 --> 00:34:10,666
Don't worry.

496
00:34:10,691 --> 00:34:12,565
We'll be seeing
plenty of each other anyway.

497
00:34:12,590 --> 00:34:13,716
No, I can't.

498
00:34:13,859 --> 00:34:16,036
Come on.
You'll get to pay me back.

499
00:34:16,625 --> 00:34:17,879
I'll even charge you interest.

500
00:34:19,570 --> 00:34:22,755
Okay. I hope
the interest isn't too high.

501
00:34:53,645 --> 00:34:57,554
You know, you're really beautiful
when you're drunk.

502
00:34:59,019 --> 00:35:01,147
You're beautiful
even when you're sober.

503
00:35:02,051 --> 00:35:06,015
Then may I kiss
the beautiful lady?

504
00:36:53,694 --> 00:36:56,913
Then you have to take care of me.

505
00:36:56,938 --> 00:36:59,318
Drunk girls need someone
to look after them.

506
00:37:00,163 --> 00:37:01,576
Kiss first. Kiss!

507
00:37:21,984 --> 00:37:24,805
Oh, Nana...

508
00:37:42,208 --> 00:37:44,932
I've read through
the plan you sent me.

509
00:37:45,107 --> 00:37:48,085
Could you
walk me through it again?

510
00:37:49,293 --> 00:37:51,757
I don't see a golf course
as just a place.

511
00:37:51,947 --> 00:37:54,934
I see it as an ecosystem where
different groups are connected.

512
00:37:55,034 --> 00:37:59,987
Customers, pros, staff, caddies,
housekeepers, groundskeepers...

513
00:38:00,012 --> 00:38:01,944
Everyone is part of
that ecosystem.

514
00:38:02,333 --> 00:38:03,341
Okay.

515
00:38:04,214 --> 00:38:05,992
I've broken it down
into four simple steps.

516
00:38:06,904 --> 00:38:09,323
First, we make sure our staff
are prepared

517
00:38:09,348 --> 00:38:11,180
to handle any situation.

518
00:38:11,346 --> 00:38:15,377
Then we get people
to see our course in a new light.

519
00:38:15,402 --> 00:38:17,259
We give them value
for their money

520
00:38:17,330 --> 00:38:20,014
and quality time
while they're here with us.

521
00:38:20,385 --> 00:38:24,432
And finally, we focus
on how our customers feel,

522
00:38:24,457 --> 00:38:28,063
because the emotional experience
matters most.

523
00:38:32,542 --> 00:38:37,899
The heart of a golf course
is L-O-V-E.

524
00:38:38,023 --> 00:38:40,285
L is Local First.

525
00:38:40,348 --> 00:38:42,674
We take care of
our own people first.

526
00:38:42,699 --> 00:38:45,084
O is Open Experience.

527
00:38:45,189 --> 00:38:47,903
We offer experiences
that go beyond just playing golf.

528
00:38:47,982 --> 00:38:50,215
V is Value Over Price.

529
00:38:50,462 --> 00:38:52,877
We create value that goes beyond
getting your money's worth.

530
00:38:52,902 --> 00:38:55,125
E is Emotional Connection.

531
00:38:55,150 --> 00:38:58,572
We build an emotional connection
with everyone who comes here.

532
00:39:02,257 --> 00:39:03,262
Love...

533
00:39:05,416 --> 00:39:06,448
What was that?

534
00:39:07,820 --> 00:39:13,713
Oh, it just sounds a lot like
something someone once told me.

535
00:39:14,200 --> 00:39:16,973
"Local First." Take care of
our own people first.

536
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:28,810
The watermelon is sweet.

537
00:39:36,507 --> 00:39:37,560
No, thanks.

538
00:39:39,925 --> 00:39:41,579
Please, enjoy yourself.

539
00:39:56,329 --> 00:39:59,454
Everyone, could I have you
over here, please?

540
00:40:11,558 --> 00:40:14,947
Hi, everyone.
Let's keep things casual today.

541
00:40:15,155 --> 00:40:17,538
I put together this little party

542
00:40:17,567 --> 00:40:20,287
because I'd like to get
to know all of you better

543
00:40:20,312 --> 00:40:22,019
outside of work formalities.

544
00:40:22,044 --> 00:40:25,648
Not as boss and employees
or management and staff,

545
00:40:26,046 --> 00:40:29,248
but as one team.

546
00:40:29,273 --> 00:40:31,106
We're all part of Goodview.

547
00:40:31,558 --> 00:40:34,254
I'm still very new
to all of this,

548
00:40:34,279 --> 00:40:37,686
so I'm asking
for everyone's support.

549
00:40:37,711 --> 00:40:41,936
Let's work together
to make Goodview thrive again.

550
00:40:42,238 --> 00:40:43,444
Vive la vie!

551
00:40:46,423 --> 00:40:48,435
- Huh?
- What's that?

552
00:40:49,684 --> 00:40:51,310
It's French.

553
00:40:51,515 --> 00:40:53,940
It's kind of like
saying "Cheers!"

554
00:40:53,965 --> 00:40:57,258
Oh! Slay, slay, hip hooray!

555
00:40:57,283 --> 00:40:59,944
Everyone! Vive la vie!

556
00:40:59,969 --> 00:41:02,335
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

557
00:41:06,504 --> 00:41:08,914
I'd also like to introduce
our new manager,

558
00:41:09,121 --> 00:41:10,767
in case some of you
haven't heard.

559
00:41:10,847 --> 00:41:14,314
Nut is someone I deeply respect

560
00:41:14,339 --> 00:41:15,937
and whose abilities
I truly believe in.

561
00:41:15,962 --> 00:41:17,532
He's here to help us
run the course.

562
00:41:22,389 --> 00:41:25,962
I'm Nut. I look forward
to working with you all.

563
00:41:26,490 --> 00:41:30,545
From now on, I won't ask
any of you to work harder.

564
00:41:31,614 --> 00:41:34,671
I'll ask you to believe more.

565
00:41:35,021 --> 00:41:37,602
Believe that we can rise
to the top again.

566
00:41:37,906 --> 00:41:40,869
Believe that our quality
is still second to none.

567
00:41:41,202 --> 00:41:44,285
Believe that if we're committed
and sincere,

568
00:41:44,598 --> 00:41:46,328
our customers will feel it.

569
00:41:47,224 --> 00:41:48,336
And finally,

570
00:41:48,834 --> 00:41:52,230
believe in Miss Nana and
her new vision for this course.

571
00:41:53,516 --> 00:41:54,891
Vive la vie!

572
00:41:55,598 --> 00:41:58,084
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

573
00:42:02,070 --> 00:42:05,237
And I'd like to introduce
one more new member

574
00:42:05,262 --> 00:42:07,912
who'll help bring
our course back to life.

575
00:42:08,082 --> 00:42:11,184
Pro Jin!
Come say hello to everyone.

576
00:42:14,022 --> 00:42:16,303
Hi, everyone. I'm Pro Jin.

577
00:42:16,328 --> 00:42:18,438
I look forward
to working with you all.

578
00:42:25,815 --> 00:42:28,411
Oh, and there's one more person

579
00:42:28,436 --> 00:42:30,286
who said he'd help me out.

580
00:42:30,594 --> 00:42:33,964
I'm sure you all know
him already. August!

581
00:42:43,972 --> 00:42:45,492
Vive la vie!

582
00:42:45,517 --> 00:42:47,517
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

583
00:42:50,784 --> 00:42:52,080
That's all you're going to say?

584
00:42:52,105 --> 00:42:55,509
I believe that for anything
to turn out well,

585
00:42:55,618 --> 00:42:57,585
it has to start with our hearts.

586
00:42:57,610 --> 00:42:59,109
If we love what we do,

587
00:42:59,317 --> 00:43:01,454
we'll want to give it
our very best.

588
00:43:03,050 --> 00:43:05,696
I have to admit,

589
00:43:06,122 --> 00:43:08,493
I didn't really care much
for this course before.

590
00:43:09,017 --> 00:43:12,209
But now, I'm starting to love it.

591
00:43:12,717 --> 00:43:16,872
I want to make this course
second to none again,

592
00:43:17,070 --> 00:43:19,724
just like it was
in my grandpa and dad's time.

593
00:43:20,310 --> 00:43:24,192
And I believe
you all want the same thing.

594
00:43:24,462 --> 00:43:26,553
Because the more popular
this course becomes,

595
00:43:26,578 --> 00:43:28,428
the more people we bring in,

596
00:43:28,570 --> 00:43:31,628
the more money
we'll all have in our pockets.

597
00:43:31,785 --> 00:43:35,250
So let's make it happen together.
Vive la vie!

598
00:43:35,568 --> 00:43:38,331
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

599
00:43:40,221 --> 00:43:41,631
Now, everyone, have fun!

600
00:43:46,226 --> 00:43:47,302
How's it going?

601
00:43:52,040 --> 00:43:53,287
Thank you so much.

602
00:43:54,525 --> 00:43:56,137
I look forward
to working with you.

603
00:43:57,904 --> 00:43:59,619
You just need to stay focused.

604
00:44:00,460 --> 00:44:01,667
Nice to meet you again.

605
00:44:03,067 --> 00:44:04,075
Okay.

606
00:44:04,467 --> 00:44:05,480
Pro Vee.

607
00:44:10,254 --> 00:44:13,711
Don't drink too much.
If you get like last night again,

608
00:44:14,166 --> 00:44:15,888
you'll lose all credibility.

609
00:44:17,846 --> 00:44:20,815
Last night? What happened?

610
00:44:21,045 --> 00:44:22,299
I don't remember a thing.

611
00:44:23,235 --> 00:44:24,762
You were really drunk
last night...

612
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:26,168
Oh, never mind.

613
00:44:26,193 --> 00:44:27,962
Let's just leave last night
where it belongs.

614
00:44:27,987 --> 00:44:29,567
Just forget about it.

615
00:44:32,752 --> 00:44:35,139
Did I do okay just now?

616
00:44:35,594 --> 00:44:37,276
It was okay.

617
00:44:37,301 --> 00:44:39,684
Just okay? Come on, Pro Vee.

618
00:44:39,709 --> 00:44:42,749
Fine. You did really well.

619
00:44:42,871 --> 00:44:44,270
You won everyone over.

620
00:44:44,295 --> 00:44:47,405
If everyone believes in you
and in each other,

621
00:44:47,430 --> 00:44:49,830
that's a strong first step
for our course.

622
00:44:51,076 --> 00:44:52,759
I love the sound of that.

623
00:44:53,206 --> 00:44:54,461
"Our course."

624
00:44:58,091 --> 00:45:02,056
I want everyone to feel
like they belong here too.

625
00:45:04,103 --> 00:45:05,164
Local First.

626
00:45:05,569 --> 00:45:08,751
Exactly. Start with
our own people, like you said.

627
00:45:10,694 --> 00:45:12,042
Thank you, Pro Vee.

628
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:13,439
For what?

629
00:45:13,640 --> 00:45:14,911
For everything.

630
00:45:14,935 --> 00:45:17,308
You know what I mean.

631
00:45:18,062 --> 00:45:20,405
If our course is going
to be number one again,

632
00:45:20,430 --> 00:45:22,053
it'll be because of everyone
on the team.

633
00:45:22,950 --> 00:45:25,417
And the number one person
on that team,

634
00:45:25,892 --> 00:45:30,000
for me, is you.

635
00:45:37,253 --> 00:45:39,615
I'll go get another glass.

636
00:45:39,640 --> 00:45:41,226
A bug's gone for a swim
in this one.

637
00:46:21,734 --> 00:46:22,758
Pro Jin.

638
00:46:26,004 --> 00:46:28,162
Now that you've seen
some of your new coworkers,

639
00:46:28,187 --> 00:46:29,554
What do you think?

640
00:46:30,062 --> 00:46:31,530
What's there to say?

641
00:46:33,586 --> 00:46:35,128
Can you hold your liquor?

642
00:46:36,826 --> 00:46:39,247
I can drink till morning.
Never been drunk.

643
00:46:43,043 --> 00:46:44,186
Bottoms up.

644
00:46:46,114 --> 00:46:49,315
Once I get started,
I'm hard to stop.

645
00:46:50,393 --> 00:46:51,757
Then why stop?

646
00:46:53,091 --> 00:46:56,392
- Well...
- I go all in on everything.

647
00:46:57,157 --> 00:46:59,040
Nothing's ever been able
to stop me.

648
00:47:02,666 --> 00:47:06,245
Then I wonder what kind of person
could stop you.

649
00:47:07,178 --> 00:47:08,384
Hmm...

650
00:47:09,630 --> 00:47:11,666
Someone who's not
afraid of me, I guess.

651
00:47:12,341 --> 00:47:15,827
Haven't met one yet, though.

652
00:47:31,310 --> 00:47:34,005
Top me up, will you?
I'm going to the restroom.

653
00:47:55,475 --> 00:47:56,712
Long time no see.

654
00:48:02,424 --> 00:48:03,999
You haven't changed at all.

655
00:48:05,015 --> 00:48:08,074
Still the beautiful golfer.

656
00:48:08,653 --> 00:48:11,180
Sweet. Sincere.

657
00:48:13,095 --> 00:48:16,142
Nana told me she's been
taking lessons from you.

658
00:48:17,435 --> 00:48:20,807
You're good. You figured
her out pretty quickly.

659
00:48:21,676 --> 00:48:23,534
Funny how I couldn't figure out
my own friend

660
00:48:23,559 --> 00:48:24,994
before she betrayed me,

661
00:48:25,267 --> 00:48:26,998
even after knowing her
for so long.

662
00:48:28,618 --> 00:48:30,888
You're still hung up on that?

663
00:48:31,231 --> 00:48:33,231
It's not something
you can just forget.

664
00:48:33,705 --> 00:48:35,522
If you want to hear
the whole story,

665
00:48:35,547 --> 00:48:37,848
- we can talk about it honestly.
- Honestly?

666
00:48:38,495 --> 00:48:40,495
Since when are you
honest with anyone?

667
00:48:41,726 --> 00:48:42,928
Thanks, though.

668
00:48:44,436 --> 00:48:45,932
You taught me one thing.

669
00:48:46,830 --> 00:48:49,674
There's no such thing
as a true friend on the fairway.

670
00:49:00,075 --> 00:49:05,149
Tonight, let's have
as much fun as we can,

671
00:49:05,174 --> 00:49:08,343
because tomorrow,
we fight together.

672
00:49:08,765 --> 00:49:10,599
For Miss Nana.

673
00:49:13,889 --> 00:49:18,853
And for Vive la vie!

674
00:49:19,745 --> 00:49:23,448
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

675
00:49:23,473 --> 00:49:26,598
♪ It's plain to see ♪

676
00:49:26,878 --> 00:49:28,878
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

677
00:49:28,903 --> 00:49:32,254
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

678
00:49:34,107 --> 00:49:35,489
My sister's gotta dance!

679
00:49:36,260 --> 00:49:38,069
She's wildin'! She's wildin'!

680
00:49:38,645 --> 00:49:40,645
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

681
00:49:40,670 --> 00:49:43,439
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

682
00:49:43,464 --> 00:49:45,245
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

683
00:49:45,270 --> 00:49:48,142
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

684
00:49:48,167 --> 00:49:51,059
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

685
00:49:51,084 --> 00:49:54,681
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

686
00:49:54,706 --> 00:49:56,706
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

687
00:49:56,731 --> 00:49:59,759
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

688
00:49:59,784 --> 00:50:03,255
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

689
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:07,957
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

690
00:50:07,982 --> 00:50:09,982
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

691
00:50:28,621 --> 00:50:30,805
Miss Nana! We have a problem!

692
00:50:31,060 --> 00:50:32,456
Marketing just told me

693
00:50:32,481 --> 00:50:35,244
all the tour groups booked
with us have canceled.

694
00:50:35,269 --> 00:50:40,054
Miss Nana! Miss Nana!
I have something to tell you.

695
00:50:40,193 --> 00:50:41,211
What is it, Chef Queen?

696
00:50:41,450 --> 00:50:44,180
My kitchen was very clean
this morning.

697
00:50:44,205 --> 00:50:45,897
Well, that's good, isn't it?

698
00:50:45,922 --> 00:50:48,306
No! By "clean," I mean...

699
00:50:48,331 --> 00:50:51,466
I walked in and the staff,
the chefs...

700
00:50:51,510 --> 00:50:54,373
everyone in the kitchen had quit!

701
00:50:54,398 --> 00:50:56,471
- What? Why?
- I have no idea!

702
00:50:56,496 --> 00:50:59,561
Yesterday's staff party
went so well.

703
00:50:59,586 --> 00:51:00,886
How did this happen overnight?

704
00:51:00,911 --> 00:51:03,420
- Did I do something wrong?
- Nana.

705
00:51:05,907 --> 00:51:08,704
Don't tell me
more people have quit.

706
00:51:08,729 --> 00:51:10,729
More than half our caddies
are gone.

707
00:51:13,938 --> 00:51:16,027
This can't be a coincidence.

708
00:51:26,018 --> 00:51:27,113
That damn March.

709
00:51:29,528 --> 00:51:30,861
Easy, Miss Nana.

710
00:51:31,127 --> 00:51:34,260
I'm not giving up that easily.
And I'm not scared.

711
00:51:34,285 --> 00:51:36,554
Because I still have all of you
ready to fight with me.

712
00:51:37,829 --> 00:51:39,003
I'm with you.

713
00:51:40,066 --> 00:51:41,087
So am I.

714
00:51:41,587 --> 00:51:42,619
Me too.

715
00:51:44,392 --> 00:51:45,479
Count me in, Sis.

716
00:51:48,293 --> 00:51:49,351
Me too.

717
00:51:51,240 --> 00:51:52,510
I'm in too.

718
00:51:53,543 --> 00:51:54,753
Vive la vie.

719
00:51:56,333 --> 00:51:57,398
Everyone...

720
00:51:58,168 --> 00:52:00,684
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

721
00:52:17,322 --> 00:52:20,532
Hi, Fahsai. This is my team.

722
00:52:20,730 --> 00:52:21,786
And this is Pro Vee.

723
00:52:21,850 --> 00:52:24,363
Someone's already signed up
for golf lessons.

724
00:52:24,388 --> 00:52:27,087
And they're having lunch together
right now.

725
00:52:27,271 --> 00:52:29,660
- Feeling possessive?
- Jealous.

726
00:52:32,754 --> 00:52:34,905
You hold a golf club every day.

727
00:52:34,930 --> 00:52:37,415
How are your hands still so soft?

728
00:52:37,619 --> 00:52:40,419
I'll have one of the staff
carry over some colored drinks

729
00:52:40,444 --> 00:52:43,334
and accidentally spill them.

730
00:52:43,359 --> 00:52:45,201
That should keep those two apart.

731
00:52:48,936 --> 00:52:53,182
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

732
00:52:53,964 --> 00:52:58,754
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

733
00:52:59,064 --> 00:53:03,479
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

734
00:53:04,196 --> 00:53:08,770
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

735
00:53:09,256 --> 00:53:14,444
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

736
00:53:14,469 --> 00:53:18,647
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

737
00:53:19,464 --> 00:53:22,659
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

738
00:53:22,684 --> 00:53:25,137
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

739
00:53:25,162 --> 00:53:30,745
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

740
00:53:30,770 --> 00:53:33,854
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

741
00:53:33,879 --> 00:53:38,794
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

742
00:53:39,986 --> 00:53:43,149
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

743
00:53:43,174 --> 00:53:45,770
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

744
00:53:45,795 --> 00:53:51,468
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

745
00:53:51,493 --> 00:53:54,692
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

746
00:53:54,717 --> 00:53:57,038
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

747
00:53:57,063 --> 00:54:00,826
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

748
00:54:02,902 --> 00:54:08,089
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

749
00:54:08,114 --> 00:54:13,115
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

750
00:54:13,140 --> 00:54:16,944
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪
